 "outline": [
  "A retired referee settles a feud between an old woman who bangs her ceiling and the boy upstairs who stomps. He rules: nothing after nine. ENDS ON: the boy knocks at his door at ten past nine, whispering that she did not knock back.",
  "The old woman sits in silence: the bangs and stomps were their goodnight. The building backs the ruling and the referee cannot say sorry. ENDS ON: the old woman announces she is moving out tomorrow.",
  "He overrules himself, sits in the third chair for the first time and restores the goodnight. That night the whole building knocks back to him."
